            <ArticleTitle>[Effectiveness of the GlideScope video laryngoscope in a case of unexpected difficult airway due to lingual tonsil hypertrophy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>289-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.redar.2014.09.011</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0034-9356(14)00273-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lingual tonsil hypertrophy can cause varying degrees of airway obstruction and is considered a risk factor for difficult mask ventilation and tracheal intubation. We report a case of unexpected difficult airway in a patient with unknown lingual tonsil hypertrophy that was solved with the use of the GlideScope video laryngoscope.</AbstractText>
